special_abilities:
  - name: "P.P.E. Channeling"
    description: "As the Knight of the White Rose. Holding a simple electronic device (flashlight, radio, video camera, portable computer, translator, shaver) runs it at no P.P.E. cost. Recharging: one small S.D.C. battery per level for 1 P.P.E. total; a car-sized battery 2; a standard E-Clip 12; a long E-Clip 18; an energy canister or rail gun 30; one shot of a heavy energy cannon (two shots if it does 6D6 to 1D4x10 M.D.) 30; a P.P.E. Clip 60."
  - name: "Fire Energy Bolts"
    description: "As the Knight of the White Rose: 4D6 M.D. blue bolts from the hands or eyes, +1D6 at levels 4, 8 and 12, range 1000 ft (305 m). 5 P.P.E. per blast, and 10 P.P.E. more buys another 1000 ft (305 m) of range."
  - name: "Steal & Redirect Ley Line Energy"
    description: "As the Knight of the White Rose. Blocks others from drawing ley line energy along a 50 ft (15.2 m) stretch per level. At an eclipse, solstice, ritual or similar time of power he can divert 1D6x10% of a mage''s summoned energy into himself at the key moment and cast with it, provided he knows who is drawing, can see them, and is within 200 ft (61 m). Stolen energy keeps ten minutes per level; any excess over his normal capacity then bleeds away harmlessly. He draws twice the usual P.P.E. at ley lines and nexus points."
  - name: "Impervious to Energy"
    description: "As the Knight of the White Rose: no damage from lasers, ion blasts, particle beams, plasma, electricity, fire, heat or radiation. Magical energy and Ley Line Storms do half damage. Rune weapons, most magic weapons, and kinetic attacks of every kind - blades, clubs, bullets, arrows, Vibro-Blades, thrown objects, falls, punches - do full damage."
  - name: "Ley Line Walker Abilities"
    description: "As the Knight of the White Rose: senses ley lines and magic energy, and has Ley Line Phasing and Ley Line Rejuvenation, as the Ley Line Walker (RUE p.113, Rifts RPG p.83)."
  - name: "Rolled O.C.C. bonuses"
    description: "The Knight of the White Rose''s combat training, which the Keeper shares: +1D4 to P.S. and +1D6+10 to Spd, on top of the fixed bonuses. Rolled bonuses, so they live here rather than in bonuses."
  - name: "Intuitive Spell Knowledge"
    description: "After three days of fasting and meditation, or of tireless work tending a garden or crops, the new Keeper simply knows thirteen spells, cast permanently at these book costs [P.P.E.]: Tongues [12], Purification of food and water [20], Negate Poison [5], Magic Shield [6], Heal Wounds [10], Globe of Daylight [2], Extinguish Fire [4], Cure Illness [15], Cure Minor Disorder [10], Cleanse [6], Breathe without Air [5], Aura of Death [12], Armor of Ithan [10]."
  - name: "Learning New Spells"
    description: "One new spell at each level after the first, chosen from Earth Warlock magic of levels 1-4, favouring growth, plants and life. A Keeper can never be taught spells or buy them. Keepers may use Techno-Wizard devices, magic weapons, armor and rune weapons."
restrictions:
