  - "Spells cannot be taught to or bought by a Keeper; new ones come only from the level-up picks."
  - "Cybernetics: none, avoided at all costs."
extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 29: Madhaven printed 35-38 (cache p036-p039): the class opens on printed 35, the White Rose section runs 35-37, the Keeper''s abilities are on 37, and the Stats block (attributes, skills, equipment) runs onto printed 38 before the notable knights. XP ladder ''Knight of the White Rose & Keeper of the Garden'', printed 79. Abilities 1-7 are printed as identical to the White Knight''s own and were transcribed from that class''s page (printed 27-28): channeling, 4D6 bolts, steal and redirect, imperviousness, the Masters of Combat bonuses, Ley Line Walker abilities and the 2D4x10 + P.E. P.P.E. pool. The Knight''s #12 (the Squire link) is outside 1-7 and is not carried. Spell names follow the catalog: Breathe Without Air, Cure Minor Disorders, Negate Poison/Toxin and Purification; the book''s costs are in the Intuitive Spell Knowledge ability. The per-level Earth Warlock pick is a named list of the 37 Earth: spells of levels 1-4 in the catalog on 2026-09-24; the preference for growth and plant spells is a note, not enforced. The Appraise Goods bonus is conditional and not added. The rolled +1D4 P.S. and +1D6+10 Spd are prose. The White Rose itself - its healing properties and prices - is not stored here; the healing items the Keeper starts with (two petals, three leaves and one thorn per level, three healing potions, two negate-poison potions, one vampire-bite salve and one super-healing potion) are stored as starting equipment at level-one quantities; the book''s two negate-poison potions are the White Rose Elixir, which negates all poisons. The per-level petals, leaves and thorn are prose. occ_group magic: printed 37 files the Keeper among the magic O.C.C.s, as printed 28 does the Mystic Knight."
