# Keeper of the Garden

## Lore

The Keepers are the Order of the White Rose''s gardeners: Knights who look after
the Garden where the Order lives, work its fields and stables alongside the
Squires, and turn their psychic and magical gifts to guarding it against the
Entities of the ruins, bandits and invaders. Above all they guard the White
Rose. They learned its care from the people of Bloom, some of whom still help
them and train new Keepers, but it is the Keepers who decide how the Rose is
used and who receives it. Tending it has given them a line of magic devoted to
healing and growing things.

Among the guilds they are highly respected, cooperate readily with the others,
and are known for their kindness, their healing and their concern for the
Order''s future and for the people of Bloom.

## The White Rose

An alien rose, apparently, that passes for an ordinary Earth rose bush until a
botanist, an Earth Warlock or a Bio-Wizard looks closely and sees the magic
running through it. It never suffers blight or pests, so every leaf and petal
looks flawless. Its healing power is among the strongest known anywhere. Only
a few beings know of it at all, and only the Knights of the White Rose are aware
that it still grows on Rifts Earth; if that got out, Atlantis, the Federation of
Magic and many others would come for it, and anyone carrying a single petal
could be hunted for the secret.

It is very hard to grow. Wild patches are small and a bloom needs five years or
more to mature, which makes the Garden''s two dozen flourishing bushes a
wonder. The leaves, sap, thorns, petals and whole flowers each have their own
healing uses and prices, recorded for the gear rows that will carry them.

## Race

No restriction. Most Keepers are human; about 10% are D-Bees.

## Equipment

Beyond the kit above: 50 ft (15.2 m) of strong cord or rope, three weeks of
food rations, a watering can (printed twice), and pruning clippers; the note
pad may be a sketch book instead, and the shovel is a folding one. Armor is the
standard light body armor, but any armor may be worn in battle or in the
Garden''s defence. Weapons: a Mutant Bone Sickle or Axe, a TW magic weapon
the Keeper chooses, a silver-plated dagger, and one weapon per W.P. with 1D6+6 spare
E-Clips for each. White Rose healing: two petals, three leaves and one thorn
per level of experience, three healing potions, two negate-poison potions, one
vampire-bite salve and one super-healing potion; the Keeper may draw on all of
the Rose''s remedies but only to help others, never for gain. Transportation is
a horse in M.D.C. barding or some exotic mount; Keepers choose their
mounts first and would rather ride than drive. Besides the credits, 2D6x1000
credits'' worth of pre-Rifts artifacts, and the healing itself is worth a
fortune. Keepers prefer barter, which leaves no trail.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'keeper-of-the-garden');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'keeper-of-the-garden';

